<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vorarlberg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vorarlberg is the westernmost state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, lying between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-constance">Lake Constance</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and the Arlberg pass, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bregenz">Bregenz</a>. It was formed from lordships of the counts of Montfort, Werdenberg and Hohenems acquired by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> between 1363 and 1765, and was long governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrol">Tyrol</a>. In 1919 a large majority voted to join <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, but the plan was not carried out.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vorarlberg.jpg" alt="Vorarlberg" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Salzburg,_Vienna,_Vorarlberg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
